      altTranslation: "Before the learned perish — doing what is blameworthy, becoming sinners —\nlike a sand-well that seeps as much as it is touched:\nif you join the sacred waters of resolute Araṅkan,\nwho blazes as a bright flame in unattached liberation, growing and driving out darkness —\nthe words Toṇṭaraṭippoṭi has spoken — it will be well.",
      theme: "Opening Salvo — the poem opens not with praise but with a warning to the learned: before you die in sin, seek the Lord of Araṅkam. Knowledge without devotion is worthless.",
