      altTranslation: "Even overrun by diseases of desire, eyes ruined —\none can still bring fragrant flowers and worship.\nBut if the heart longing for Araṅkan's feet is lost —\nit will be as if no one exists in a family of worth.\n\nHe who is the inner meaning of the Oṃ-bearing Veda,\nwho has claimed me without ceasing —\nshe who stands as a flame of austerity on the chest\nof self-contained Araṅkan.",
      theme: "The One Irreplaceable Thing — sickness can be borne; blindness can be borne. But losing the heart's longing for the Lord is the true death. The Lord is the Veda's inner meaning.",
