      transliteration: "Nāliṉ naṉṟu āvatu\nāraṇatt tamiḻ ivai\nāliṉ kīḻ uraittāṉ\nñāṉa muṉi aṭi\nvēliṉ kūrmai pōl\nviṭuvāṉ viṇai keṭṭu\nkāliṟkē caraṇ āvēṉ\nkali yuka muṉivaṉē.",
      english: "Better than the four — these Tamil Vedas.\nThe feet of the sage of wisdom who spoke under the banyan tree.\nLike the sharpness of a spear, releasing karma to be destroyed —\nI shall take refuge at the feet:\nO sage of the Kali age!",
      tamilUrai: "நாலின் நன்று ஆவது — நான்கு வேதங்களைவிட நன்றானது. ஆரணத் தமிழ் இவை — தமிழ் வேதங்கள் (திருவாய்மொழி). ஆலின் கீழ் உரைத்தான் ஞான முனி அடி — ஆலமர செல்வன் (நம்மாழ்வார்) அடி. வேல் கூர்மை போல் விடுவான் வினை கெட்டு — கலி யுக முனிவனே.",
      altTranslation: "Better than the four — these Tamil Vedas.\nThe feet of the wisdom-sage who spoke under the banyan tree.\nLike spear-sharpness, releasing karma to destruction —\nI take refuge at his feet:\nO sage of the Kali age!",
      theme: "The Tamil Vedas Surpass the Sanskrit Vedas — a bold claim made directly: these Tamil Vedas (Nammāḻvār's Tiruvāymoḻi) are better than the four Sanskrit Vedas.",
      note: "Nāliṉ naṉṟu āvatu āraṇatt tamiḻ ivai — 'better than the four, these Tamil Vedas' — is one of the most explicit statements of Tamil canonical pride in the entire Divya Prabandham. Nammāḻvār is called the sage who spoke under the banyan tree (ālam — the tamarind tree at Āḻvārtirunagari) and the sage of the Kali age — because the Kali age, though generally bad, produced Nammāḻvār, which makes it the best of ages."
